Objective

Exploit a client-side prototype pollution vulnerability to achieve DOM-based Cross-Site Scripting (DOM XSS).

In this lab, the application attempts to protect itself against prototype pollution by filtering dangerous property names such as:

__proto__
constructor
prototype

However, the sanitization mechanism is not applied recursively. This allows the blacklist to be bypassed by manipulating the structure of the property name.

The prototype pollution can then be combined with a JavaScript gadget that uses the inherited transport_url property as the source of a dynamically created <script> element.

The complete exploitation chain is:

Prototype Pollution Filter Bypass
            ↓
Object.prototype.transport_url
            ↓
config.transport_url
            ↓
script.src
            ↓
JavaScript execution
            ↓
DOM XSS
